{A.1 = 1-8}
11=1.	Lord, perfect in august wisdom and recognised for his mighty counsel, 
15=2.	@wDN{Ḫaia}, who holds the great tablets, 
19=3.	who enriches the deep wisdom! Accountant of Ḫal-an-kug, 
23=4.	having the final overview of the arts of @wDN{Nisaba's} house of wisdom; palace archivist of heaven and earth, 
27=5.	who keeps count of every single assignment, who holds a holy reed-stylus and covers the great tablets of destiny with writing! 
31=6.	Wise one, who prompts holy @wDN{An} with words and attention at the appropriate times; 
35=7.	seal-holder of Father @wDN{Enlil}! He who brings forth the holy objects from the treasure-house of @wTN{E-kur}; 
39=8.	ornament of the @fsux{abzu} shrine, wearing his hair loose for Lord @wDN{Nudimmud}! 

{A.9 = 9-20}
43=9.	@wDN{Ḫaia}, linen-clad priest of @wTN{E-unir}, who stocks the holy @fsux{uzga} precinct; learned scholar of the shrine @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}, whose august name is great, whose mind is discerning; who dwells in the great dining-hall alongside the maiden @wDN{Ningal}! Fair of features, beloved spouse of @wDN{Nun-bar-še-gunu} and augustly renowned father-in-law of Father @wDN{Enlil}, the Great Mountain; junior administrator, possessor of wisdom, acknowledged in heaven and earth, who receives the tribute for the gods, the abundance of mountains and seas! Interpreter of the obscurity of @wDN{Enlil's} (?) words, skilful one who steers the august princely divine powers, with …… girt at his side! Formed (?) with a broad heart, holding in his hands the holy divine plans of the temple of @wSN{Eridug}, @wDN{Ḫaia}, who wears the ceremonial robe during pure lustrations of the @fsux{engur}! @wDN{Indagara}, administrator who performs the opening of the mouth for the gods in the heavens and in the underworld, and who is versed in the meaning of obscure tablets; craftsman of the great gods! 

{A.21 = 21-28}
91=21.	He who fixes the standards on their pegs, planner (?) who artfully excavates (?) the soil of the Land, who decorates the floor and makes the dining-hall attractive for @wDN{Anšar} and the Great Mountain! Tall and with head high, he whose utterances from the @fsux{abzu} shrine are favourable, who carefully holds the pure white loaves of the house of the gods! @wDN{Kusu} and @wDN{Indagara}, without whom heaven would not be pure nor earth bright, continual providers of the great meals of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil} in their grand dining-hall! He who gazes upon the holy precinct, upon Lord @wDN{Nudimmud}; he who holds the holy bronze vessels, who makes hearts rejoice and soothes spirits! 

